Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): content::FileSystemAccessPermissionContext
on this branch still names the enum UserAction (it was renamed to
AccessTrigger upstream), so the third-party drag-and-drop check added to
GetSharedHandleStateForNonSandboxedPath() uses the existing user_action
parameter and UserAction::kDragAndDrop. Conflicting test changes
(chrome_file_system_access_permission_context_unittest.cc,
file_system_access_browsertest.cc,
file_system_access_directory_handle_impl_unittest.cc) are dropped as
test-only drift. The chrome/ permission-context hunk is mirrored into
Electron's own copy in a separate commit.

